ain-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972068#post972068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tha Dark Mother. Beasts are not &quot;as &quot; the Dark Mother <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I read you post: is not require to repeat and repeat, thanks you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is directly from the Nightmare section, stating that nightmares do, in fact, affect creatures immune to fear.<br /> You might have read what I said, but you obviously didn't understand it, because you're still acting like this issue is real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 09-18-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:33:48-07:00","id":972070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972069#post972069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is directly from the Nightmare section, stating that nightmares do, in fact, affect creatures immune to fear.<br /> You might have read what I said, but you obviously didn't understand it, because you're still acting like this issue is real.<br /> <br /> Seriously - maybe you should read the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could say the same thing about you: have you read the merit? I know that you read it.<br /> I see a conflict about two source that say opposite point.<br /> I repeat: i have read your point.<br /> And be more polite can be a good thing too.<br /> I dont question your ability to read and understand a written text.<br /> Be polite you too, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:36:20-07:00","id":972072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972070#post972070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could say the same thing about you: have you read the merit? I know that you read it.<br /> I see a conflict about two source that say opposite point.<br /> I repeat: i have read your point.<br /> And be more polite can be a good thing too.<br /> I dont question your ability to read and understand a written text.<br /> Be polite you too, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule in Beast exists to specifically counter creatures that are immune to fear.<br /> The merit is a general merit that makes a creature immune to fear.<br /> <br /> There's no conflicting rules. The Beast rule <b>exists</b> because of situations like the one the merit presents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:37:46-07:00","id":972073,"title":"","content":"Or merit trump too the beast premise about nightmare.<br /> The merit say exactly this.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:39:18-07:00","id":972074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972073#post972073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or merit trump too the beast premise about nightmare.<br /> The merit say exactly this.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. It doesn't say that it grants immunity to fear AND immunity to powers that work even against creatures that are immune to fear.<br /> It just grants immunity to fear. There's no second layer that goes above and beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:48:00-07:00","id":972077,"title":"","content":"Beast doesn't say it overcomes special abilities that grant immunity to fear. The line you keep quoting is referring to the fact that Nightmares work on supernaturals, not just mortals.<br /> <br /> 'Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don't dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother.' Note, can, not 'will always.'<br /> <br /> Just use the Merit as is. If you really need to have someone magically scare your mage, remember the last line, 'Should the attempts to frighten you play off of Conditions or vices you already suffer from, you <i>are </i>vulnerable, but treat your Composure as two dots higher than it is.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:48:55-07:00","id":972078,"title":"","content":"Nofather Ninja!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972077#post972077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast doesn't say it overcomes special abilities that grant immunity to fear. The line you keep quoting is referring to the fact that Nightmares work on supernaturals, not just mortals.<br /> <br /> 'Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don't dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother.' Note, can, not 'will always.'<br /> <br /> Just use the Merit as is. If you really need to have someone magically scare your mage, remember the last line, 'Should the attempts to frighten you play off of Conditions or vices you already suffer from, you <i>are </i>vulnerable, but treat your Composure as two dots higher than it is.'</div> </div> </div> </div>...Or a clash of wills? This could be an idea too.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Merit grant immunity to all magical fear induced terror.<br /> By default.<br /> The merit grant an extra protection: it is not assumed that one line of text take care of all the other merit and power of the other line, ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:55:15-07:00","id":972080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972077#post972077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don't dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother.' Note, can, not 'will always.'<br /> '</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they won't <i>always </i>work on anything. That's what the dice rolls are for. The merit is supernatural in nature, and grants immunity to fear.<br /> <br /> It by <i>definition</i> turns the user into a 'creature that doesn't feel fear.'<br /> If you want to treat that differently from other supernatural resistances some creatures have to the abilities, go for it, but it really doesn't seem like the intent.<br /> <br /> The line is obviously there to make sure that these kinds of ridiculous arguments don't come up. The answer to 'Can I void an entire suite of abilities of a splat with minimal investment / by being a special snowflake' is obviously no.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> You don't seem to want to let a 3 dot merit totally void an entire suit of abilities.<br /> You've been given a clear out to avoid doing so, per the book that suite of abilities are from.<br /> <br /> You're continuing to argue that it <i>should</i> work.<br /> Why did you start this thread? Because it doesn't look like you're interested in the common-sense, book-supported answer.<br /> <br /> This is how the interaction <i>should </i>work:<br /> <br /> Beast: *uses a psychic attack based on fear*<br /> Deadpan Dude: Ha! I have a merit that says I'm not afraid of you!<br /> Beast: Ha! My power explicitly works even if you're not afraid of me!<br /> Deadpan dude has nothing else to come back with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:58:14-07:00","id":972084,"title":"","content":"My ...<br /> The thread was not a battle with you over the last word... it was about an opinion about OTHER venue. You give me a single venue, valid too!<br /> I read it and want more venue, sorry if your idea is not the most holy for me... i am totally sick now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T13:02:04-07:00","id":972086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972084#post972084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ...<br /> The thread was not a battle with you over the last word... it was about an opinion about OTHER venue. You give me a single venue, valid too!<br /> I read it and want more venue, sorry if your idea is not the most holy for me... i am totally sick now.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to let the merit work, but don't want it to be a complete and total void, then nofather's reminder that playing off of Conditions and Vices works against that merit is a good solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:15:50-07:00","id":972152,"title":"","content":"Easy solution, if you find it problematic, don't allow it in your Chronicle. Just because my Mages players have the option to dump merits to gain gnosis before the game begins in the book doesn't mean I allow it in a Chronicle if it doesn't fit with the beginning wherein the players are only awakening during the first session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:50:00-07:00","id":972238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972077#post972077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don't dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother.' Note, can, not 'will always.'</div> </div> </div> </div>When you use a Nightmare on somebody, you're bringing a piece of the Primordial Dream into sympathy with them. The contents of the Nightmare don't have to be scary to be metaphysically touching you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:12:12-07:00","id":972249,"title":"","content":"All the merit does in regards to Beasts is make the mortal hard to feed from.<br /> <br /> Most nightmares are created FROM fears, but don't actually directly cause fear, they create situations that are scary, but they don't magically enduce fear directly.<br /> <br /> It would defeat the purpose if they did. Its mean to scare you by its horrifying nature, not magically induce the emotion of fear in someone.<br /> <br /> To put it in another way, Nightmares give the target something to be afraid of, but it doesn't compel someone to be afraid.<br /> <br /> What does it do? It blocks magic that causes fear or disgust. So it blocks magic that directly trigger emotions of fear and disgust, like the Changeling contract Paralyzing Shudder, or a high Wyrd Changeling using Bedlam to induce fear, but it doesn't stop a Changeling from creating Illusions and effects intended to scare you or creating Nightmarish dreams (although they won't scare, the dream itself can be created, it just doesn't work as intended).<br /> <br /> Also the merit has an inherient exception for stuff that connects with your vice or conditions, so if you have greed as your vice, and something tries to scare you into believing that you've lost all you life savings, that magic can still work on you to scare you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:37:36-07:00","id":972256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972238#post972238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you use a Nightmare on somebody, you're bringing a piece of the Primordial Dream into sympathy with them. The contents of the Nightmare don't have to be scary to be metaphysically touching you.</div> </div> </div> </div>And with the Deadpan Merit, 'you've slipped free of horror itself; no matter what the Fallen World throws at you, you can meet it calmly.' I suppose in the final edition it might make an exception for the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> What is the problem with this Merit? It doesn't make one immune to Beasts. It does make one fairly immune to one vampire Discipline, a natural ability of werewolves and some ephemerals, resistant to some Mind spells and one of Beasts power sets. Certainly, if your game is about mages versus Beasts this would be useful, but even then it wouldn't necessarily make or break the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-18-2016, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:17:13-07:00","id":972281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972256#post972256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And with the Deadpan Merit, 'you've slipped free of horror itself; no matter what the Fallen World throws at you, you can meet it calmly.' I suppose in the final edition it might make an exception for the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> What is the problem with this Merit? It doesn't make one immune to Beasts. It does make one fairly immune to one vampire Discipline, a natural ability of werewolves and some ephemerals, resistant to some Mind spells and one of Beasts power sets. Certainly, if your game is about mages versus Beasts this would be useful, but even then it wouldn't necessarily make or break the game.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again it doesn't make you immune to a subset of Beast Powers, Beast Nightmare are designed to inspire fear and are inspired by it, but they don't compel it and feeling fear is not required for them to work. I suggest you reread the Nightmares individually to figure out what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:01:20-07:00","id":972298,"title":"","content":"Umm...so how does no being afraid protect you from the gaze of the Gorgon turning you to stone? It's isn't a fear effect.<br /> Or a seductive beast using a nightmare to put you into a Wanton state? That's not fear either. Not all nightmares cause fear so this merit wouldn't effect all nightmare just the ones that cause fear effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:52:46-07:00","id":972318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972054#post972054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you do interpret it as granting immunity to Nightmares, that doesn't seem so bad. Depending on whether the Beast in question is a PC or not, putting an embodiment of primordial terror against someone who can look them in the eye and say &quot;I'm not afraid of you&quot; sounds like a feature, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until said beast gives them proper cause to fear it by disemboweling their friends with invisible talons. <b>*shrug*</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:03:44-07:00","id":972326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972281#post972281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again it doesn't make you immune to a subset of Beast Powers, Beast Nightmare are designed to inspire fear and are inspired by it, but they don't compel it and feeling fear is not required for them to work. I suggest you reread the Nightmares individually to figure out what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, everyone.<br /> <br /> As much as I don't like Beast, Deadpan does nothing against their powers, other than leave you unafraid of them. You still suffer the hallucinations or whatever, but they don't really <i>horrify</i> you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:05:10-07:00","id":972327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972318#post972318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until said beast gives them proper cause to fear it by disemboweling their friends with invisible talons. <b>*shrug*</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I didn't mean to inadvertently imply that there existed a situation where a Beast would not be in complete control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:13:39-07:00","id":972332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972326#post972326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I don't like Beast, Deadpan does nothing against their powers, other than leave you unafraid of them. You still suffer the hallucinations or whatever, but they don't really <i>horrify</i> you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Being unfazed by the fact that your hair, teeth and muscle mass all fell off in an instant doesn't really changes that they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:23:10-07:00","id":972337,"title":"","content":"I thinked that the Nightmare , as mental power of Beast, were based on a soprannatural effect based upon fear.<br /> I thanks everybody for your post, i read you with pleasure!<br /> So, if i make exception from some or all, Beast mind powers, this is supported from many other peopole: that can be very insightfull for my future troup!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:27:03-07:00","id":972479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=972337#post972337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thinked that the Nightmare , as mental power of Beast, were based on a soprannatural effect based upon fear.<br /> I thanks everybody for your post, i read you with pleasure!<br /> So, if i make exception from some or all, Beast mind powers, this is supported from many other peopole: that can be very insightfull for my future troup!</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Just remember not all nightmares cause fear, or use fear based effects so that merit doesn't effect all Nightmares, just the ones that specificaly use fear as a tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:51:52-07:00","id":973365,"title":"","content":"You could always do what I do, which is either toss the Merit out altogether or rework it to give a bonus instead of an outright immunity. But in general I have big distaste for blanket immunity merits and stuff like that, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:46:59-07:00","id":973451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=973365#post973365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always do what I do, which is either toss the Merit out altogether or rework it to give a bonus instead of an outright immunity. But in general I have big distaste for blanket immunity merits and stuff like that, so.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not really blanket immunity, you just having to research your target first. If your target has the lust vice and you find out, use a nightmare about impotence and it will still work.<br /> <br /> If you target it has the swooning condition for Brad Pitt, then send them a terrorfying nightmare of being rejected by Brad Pitt in the most humiliating way and then killed by him, then it will work on your target.<br /> <br /> There are in built exceptions to the immunity, you just have to do the leg work, which is actually what makes it so interesting to use in Beast, the Dead Pan merit just ups the challenge of scaring the target. I love the merit for Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:19:37-07:00","id":973470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972039-mage-beast-issue-with-deadpan-merit?p=973451#post973451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its not really blanket immunity, you just having to research your target first. If your target has the lust vice and you find out, use a nightmare about impotence and it will still work.<br /> <br /> If you target it has the swooning condition for Brad Pitt, then send them a terrorfying nightmare of being rejected by Brad Pitt in the most humiliating way and then killed by him, then it will work on your target.<br /> <br /> There are in built exceptions to the immunity, you just have to do the leg work, which is actually what makes it so interesting to use in Beast, the Dead Pan merit just ups the challenge of scaring the target. I love the merit for Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if you know they have a vice lust you flood their mind with increasingly sexual imagery until they become light headed and unable to attack you.<br /> <br /> Or Flood their mind with Brad Pitt's death over, and over, more horrifying than the last and let them fall into depression until they can't focus any more or spend willpower. Until they point the gun at themselves to be with their beloved over the cruel separation of life. Nightmares aren't just about fear, they can cover things like so nymphonainically sexy it's scary, or so incredibly sad you feel empty inside. Dead Pan only protects them from fear so don't attack fear attack the other emotions or mental effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}